## Raster sidecar
Every record carries `raster` + top-level `gate_snn` + `gate_compute`. Windows {wins[0]:.0f}/{wins[1]:.0f}/{wins[2]:.0f} ms; `window_s == window_ms/1000` exactly; `spikes == round(neurons·rate·window_s)` with zero slack ({n_sp[0]}/{n_sp[1]}/{n_sp[2]} at {rates[0]}/{rates[1]}/{rates[2]} Hz over {n_neu[0]}/{n_neu[1]}/{n_neu[2]} neurons); `energy_pJ = spikes·23` and `energy_uJ = spikes·23e-6` exact ({n_sp[0]*23}/{n_sp[1]*23}/{n_sp[2]*23} pJ). Routing source/target + 3-entry tables + `third_factor` on all three (modulators {tfs[0]} / {tfs[1]} / {tfs[2]}; τe {taus[0]}/{taus[1]}/{taus[2]} s as consistent `tau_e_s`+`tau_e_ms` pairs). Excerpts integer `t_us`, in-window, `neuron_id`-bounded, sorted, full-window by construction, per-spike amplitude with adaptation (0.82**k) plus noise. ISI histograms from the full window, bins ≥1 ms, counts sum to `spikes − distinct_active_neurons` ({isis[0]}/{isis[1]}/{isis[2]}). Same-neuron gaps ≥1100 µs pre-round, ≥1000 µs serialized. `gate_snn` on all three: decisions REJECT/MODIFY/ACCEPT matching each lead trajectory; every rate-declaring population's budget exact against its decision window. `gate_compute.per_check` windows 32–40 ms, budgets exact ({gc[0]} / {gc[1]} / {gc[2]}). Main streams: {events[0]}/{events[1]}/{events[2]} events (inside the 5–40 cap), strictly increasing `t_rel_ms` only (no `t_ms` mix), same-channel refractory ≥0.8 ms (169 IRIS pair at 1.3 ms, 170 pyrometer pair at 1.2 ms, 171 OIW pair at 1.5 ms).

## Self-critique

### Edge cases added vs still thin
- **Added:** first IRIS rotating pulse-echo remaining-wall family on a hydrotreater HEX tube with a recomputable d=c·ToF/2 (`8.00 mm`) plus compression-speed identity and three-party collusion including the IRIS infra owner; first dual-wavelength ratio-pyrometer family on a BOF bath with recomputable T=k_t·I1/I2 (`1800.0 K`) and ratio identity, plus a resolved-innocent pyrometer tech (timezone-skipped lamp-cal, not last-to-badge); first UV-fluorescence oil-in-water family on a produced-water polisher with recomputable C=k_f·(I−I_bg)/I_ref (`24.00 ppm`) plus intensity-ratio identity; bounded ACCEPT whose out-of-scope clause is adjacent polishers rather than a hopper/taphole/dump cap; operational t2 on all three (HEX-soak hold, new-pyrometer restart, skip-polisher refusal); provenance trio designed/hil/simulated; 18 min / 24 min / 12 min slow floors in-stream.
- **Still thin:** (i) 169's c is a lumped 5.00 mm/us, not a temperature-dependent steel table — a thermal hop that fakes 8.00 mm inside an 18.40 mm Irisveil corridor is unwritten; (ii) 170's k_t is a lumped dual-wavelength gain, not an emissivity / slag-window map, so a slag hop that fakes 1800.0 K is unwritten; (iii) 171's k_f is a lumped UV gain, not a quenching / turbidity table, so a scatter hop that fakes 24.00 ppm inside a 4.80 last-good is unwritten; (iv) vendor-only as a *lead* REJECT on a plant with *no* independent IRIS/pyrometer/OIW installed yet remains slightly harder — 169/170 still have plant heads; (v) stream amplitudes remain authored constants (raster draws are the only seeded noise); (vi) r52 densification leftovers (T/P/ozone-flow, probe-temperature/runout, heater-bias/split-flow) and r38 leftovers (OCT group-index, DCPD current-spread, moisture-corrected impact-echo) were left for those rounds' owners.

### Realism of noise / temporal fidelity
- Strong: 169's 8.00 mm, speed identity 5.00, and 18.0 min HEX-soak (`6000+1080=7080 s`) recompute from the record; 170's 1800.0 K, ratio 4.50, and 24.0 min cooldown (`2820+1440=4260 s`) recompute; 171's 24.00 ppm, ratio 6.00, and 12.0 min survey (`6000+720=6720 s`) recompute. Raster adaptation (0.82**k plus 4% noise) and the 1.2–1.5 ms physics pairs give the 5–40 stream a raster-scale motif without violating 0.8 ms same-channel refractory.
- **Gaps, honestly:** (i) 5–40 cap still forces heavy thinning (20 Hz IRIS rotation kept as 4 ToF points; 10 Hz pyrometer ratio kept as 4 I1 points plus one I2 pair; 1 Hz UV fluorescence kept as 4 I points); (ii) 169's post-stop 10.00 mm is a later sample, not a closed-loop soak controller; (iii) 170 HIL coupon times an in-service isolate that the stream does not independently witness on a second live bath until the new pyrometer starts; (iv) no gate_snn input→output volley pair at raster resolution this round (r04-a1 already staged that).

### Training value (SNN/LSM + agentic)
Distillation targets: IRIS d=c·ToF/2 reconstruction head plus speed identity; conjunctive min-wall floor vs continue-firing vs unit trip; IRIS-infra collusion; dual-wavelength T=k_t·I1/I2 head plus ratio identity; isolate-floor heat vs keep-blowing vs shop-trip; exoneration against last-to-badge social pressure; UV-fluorescence C=k_f·(I−I_bg)/I_ref and ratio identities; bounded ACCEPT with polisher-out-of-scope; skip-isolate refusal under survey takt. Agentic value concentrates in three patterns: reconstruction-as-SoT on a physical wall/T/oil load the raw corridor cannot see, earned ACCEPT with an explicit physical out-of-scope object (P-1 and P-2), and stop-then-hold so a REJECT does not become a unit/shop/dump kill.

